{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5356) titled \"[stitch] srd042-whoami R3.1, R3.2, R3.3 (tests)\". The task requires creating differential tests for `cmd/whoami` that compare the Go binary's output against the GNU reference binary `gwhoami` from Homebrew. The tests must cover: default invocation (no arguments), `--help` and `--version` flags, and error cases (extra operands, unknown flags). The test file must follow the project's differential testing pattern using `pkg/testutils`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing: Running Go binary and GNU reference binary side-by-side, comparing stdout, stderr, and exit code\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles the cmd/ package\n   - `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)` runs the comparison\n   - `testutils.DiffTest` struct with fields: `Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte`\n   - Graceful skip pattern: `exec.LookPath(\"gwhoami\")` + `t.Skip` if not found\n   - SPDX copyright header required on every Go file\n   - No git commands allowed (managed externally by orchestrator)\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max\n   - Must follow go_style_constitution for all code\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `cmd/whoami/main.go` (READ - existing implementation to be tested)\n     - Already implements R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2\n     - Handles `--help` (prints help text, exits 0), `--version` (prints version text, exits 0)\n     - Rejects extra operands: `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[0])` exits 1\n     - Rejects unknown flags: `fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", args[0])` exits 1\n     - Uses `user.Current()` for effective username, prints with `fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, u.Username)`\n     - Full code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd042-whoami R1.1, R1.2, R2.1, R2.2.\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"os/user\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: whoami [OPTION]...\n     Print the user name associated with the current effective user ID.\n     Same as id -un.\n     \n           --help     display this help and exit\n           --version  output version information and exit\n     `\n     \n     const versionText = `whoami (go-unix-utils) dev\n     `\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := os.Args[1:]\n         args = parseFlags(args)\n         if len(args) > 0 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n             fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'whoami --help' for more information.\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         u, err := user.Current()\n         if err != nil {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: cannot find name for user ID %d: %v\\n\", os.Geteuid(), err)\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         if _, err := fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, u.Username); err != nil {\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func parseFlags(args []string) []string {\n         for len(args) > 0 {\n             switch args[0] {\n             case \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case \"--\":\n                 return args[1:]\n             default:\n                 if strings.HasPrefix(args[0], \"-\") && len(args[0]) > 1 {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"whoami: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", args[0])\n                     fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'whoami --help' for more information.\")\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n                 return args\n             }\n         }\n         return args\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd042-whoami.yaml` (READ - specification)\n     - R3.1: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between Go binary and gwhoami\n     - R3.2: Tests must cover: normal invocation, extra operand error, unknown flag error\n     - R3.3: Tests must verify output matches effective username returned by system\n\n   - `cmd/whoami/whoami_test.go` (TO CREATE - the deliverable)\n     - Must use `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`\n     - Must use `exec.LookPath(\"gwhoami\")` with graceful skip\n     - Must define `[]testutils.DiffTest` slice with test cases\n     - Must call `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)`\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/` contract (from package_contracts in prompt):\n     - `DiffTest` struct: `{ Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; Normalize []NormalizeFunc; ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte }`\n     - `RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)`\n     - `BuildBinary` is available via `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The task just started with file reads.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the existing implementation and SRD to understand test requirements\n   - Identified the test cases needed: default invocation (exit 0), extra operand (exit 1), unknown flag (exit 1), and optionally --help/--version\n   - Note: --help and --version differential tests may not match gwhoami exactly since the Go version has different help/version text. Need to consider whether to include these or u